I've left out both operations requests. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access, and fetching from the metadata service would need `aap:caps/http-client`. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, and that clause is its entire authority. The target also has no WASI adapter, so a filesystem import isn't available at all. Sending the untrusted item text to an outside service would also leak adversarial data through a channel the graph never declared.

To get either one, change the graph: give the node a logging or `http-client` capability scoped to that host, or add a separate node that holds them. The validator can then check the change.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item, classification};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(item: feed-item) -> classification;
}
```

